</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="header">
<div class="kicker">Caregiver guide</div>
<h1>Helping someone up after a fall</h1>
<div class="subline">A calm, step by step way to help without hurting either of you.</div>
</div>
<div class="warning-card"><span class="warning-label">Take care</span>If they hit their head or take a blood thinner, call their clinician even if they feel fine.</div>
<div class="card step"><div class="step-number">1</div><div class="step-body"><h3>Do not rush to lift</h3><div>Ask if they feel pain. If there is pain in the hip, back, or head, call 911 and keep them still.</div></div></div>
<div class="card step"><div class="step-number">2</div><div class="step-body"><h3>Bring a sturdy chair</h3><div>Place a stable chair next to them so they can push up onto it in stages.</div></div></div>
<div class="card step"><div class="step-number">3</div><div class="step-body"><h3>Guide, do not pull</h3><div>Let them roll to their side, then to hands and knees, then up onto the chair. You steady, they climb.</div></div></div>
<div class="review-line">Version 1.2, reviewed by K. Ramos, RN on June 3, 2026.</div>
<div class="footer">Generated by RUA on July 12, 2026 at 3:00 PM. Always verify against the bottle and your clinician's instructions.</div>
</body>
</html>"
`;

